      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, I used /usr/bin/time for measuring the duration. I considered using the Go memory profiling although it seems to me that memory usage displayed by `top` is more likely to measure the impact on the system (in case Go measures memory differently (such as not including parts of the runtime in its measurements)). I was a little concerned when I was running `top` without any arguments but when I switched to `top -d 0.1`, it updated often enough to get three significant figures matching between subsequent memory samples toward the end.",
